From 2b3bee00ba9c45f20d4fb28d99dd1219d425ac61 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ryan Ewen <ryan.ewen@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 2 Sep 2026 14:04:58 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Keep observing a subagent whose chat outlives its
 spawning turn

Subagent chat observations were owned by the parent turn's `_observeTurn` store, so
`onTurnEnded` disposed them along with the child chat subscription. When the parent
turn completes before the subagent's chat is created, that disposal sends an
`unsubscribe` while the client's `subscribe` is still in flight; the server's
post-await liveness check then fails it and the protocol handler reports it as
`Resource not found`. Nothing re-subscribes afterwards, so the subagent's tool calls
are never claimed and its turn never closes.

The same ownership breaks background subagents outright: those are designed to
outlive their parent turn, so their chat must stay observable after it ends.

Subagent observations are now handed off at turn end instead of being torn down. An
observation whose child chat is still running, or has not been created yet, moves to
a session-scoped map and is released when the subagent settles, when a live in-turn
observation supersedes it, or when the chat session is torn down. Observations whose
subagent already finished are disposed exactly as before. A detached observer stops
emitting into its parent's now-closed response, but keeps the subscription and the
tool call claim that let the subagent finish.
